#### Migration Code Example

**Before (Confluent.Kafka direct usage):**

```csharp
// Old implementation
var producerConfig = new ProducerConfig
{
    BootstrapServers = configuration["Kafka:BootstrapServers"],
    Acks = Acks.All,
    EnableIdempotence = true,
    // ... many more settings
};

using var producer = new ProducerBuilder<string, string>(producerConfig)
    .SetValueSerializer(new JsonSerializer<ClaimApprovedEvent>())
    .Build();

var message = new Message<string, string>
{
    Key = claim.Id,
    Value = JsonSerializer.Serialize(@event),
    Headers = new Headers { { "source", Encoding.UTF8.GetBytes("claims-service") } }
};

var result = await producer.ProduceAsync("claims.approved.v1", message);
```

**After (EaaS SDK):**

```csharp
// New implementation
// Program.cs - one-time registration
builder.Services.AddEventPublisher<ClaimApprovedEvent>(options =>
{
    options.Topic = "claims.approved.v1";
    options.KeySelector = evt => evt.ClaimId;
});

// Service - simplified usage
public class ClaimService
{
    private readonly IEventPublisher<ClaimApprovedEvent> _publisher;

    public ClaimService(IEventPublisher<ClaimApprovedEvent> publisher)
    {
        _publisher = publisher;
    }

    public async Task PublishEventAsync(ClaimApprovedEvent @event)
    {
        var result = await _publisher.PublishAsync(
            @event,
            key: @event.ClaimId,
            headers: new Dictionary<string, string> { ["source"] = "claims-service" });
    }
}
```

**Benefits of Migration:**
- 60-80% reduction in boilerplate code
- Automatic retry, DLQ, and observability
- Type-safe event publishing/consumption
- Simplified testing with SDK test utilities
- Automatic platform compliance

